ABL="Ableton/MIDI-friendly: the part is written as a MIDI clip; the time-compress and transpose steps are plain MIDI edits (any DAW piano roll), the resample is a bounce/freeze-and-flatten."
EARLY="If the track has drums, they enter early (~8 counts / ~12 s); only pad/texture before that (Matt's preference)."

S("EuPisVu55oU","Lo-Fi Resampling in Ableton Live [Tutorial]",
 "fifth-varispeed-resample-2-3-time-compress-up-fifth-bounce-unwarped-down-fifth-tape-texture-piano-strings",
 "Fifth-ratio varispeed resample: make clean piano/orchestral strings sound sampled-from-record by compressing the MIDI to 2/3 length, transposing up a perfect fifth, bouncing to audio and playing the audio un-warped a fifth down",
 "Give a clean sampled-instrument part (piano or orchestral strings) the coloured, tape/vinyl-sampled character of varispeed resampling while keeping its original tempo and pitch: write the part humanly in MIDI, add a spare bar, use a triplet-grid reference to scale the clip to exactly 2/3 of its length, transpose all notes +7 semitones, bounce to audio, turn warping off and transpose the audio -7 semitones (a perfect fifth is a 3:2 ratio, so slowing by 2/3 restores the original time and pitch through the sampler's resample interpolation), then group with a quiet EQ'd noise bed and gentle saturation glue. Delta vs granular/orchestral-hybrid and looper-resample variants: an exact interval-ratio varispeed round trip (time and pitch preserved) as the core trick, applied to orchestral strings as well as piano.",
 ["A DAW with MIDI clips, a resampling/bounce track and un-warped (repitch-mode) audio playback","A sampled piano and/or orchestral-strings instrument"],
 [("part","midi","An 8-bar piano or strings phrase",True),("tempo_bpm","number","Project tempo (unchanged by the process)",False)],
 [("resampled_audio","audio","Audio clip at the original tempo and pitch with varispeed/resample colouring"),("group","audio","Group of resampled part + quiet noise bed + saturation glue")],
 ["Ratio rule: time scale and transposition must match (2/3 length with +7 st, then -7 st un-warped). Other pairs work only if they match the same ratio (e.g. 1/2 length with +12 st, then -12 st).",
  "Leave out the transcript's frequency-shifter with a sample-and-hold LFO (~3 Hz random repitch). It is random pitch wobble, which Matt dislikes, so the pitch stays steady.",
  "Leave out vinyl crackle/clicks (a rapid clicking texture Matt dislikes). If a noise bed is wanted, use a smooth, low-level broadband hiss (e.g. tape hiss) high-passed and EQ'd with no ticks.",
  "Chop-and-repeat rearranging is optional and must be whole phrases/bars, not short stutter repeats.",
  "Humanising stays in timing (small flams, slightly off-grid) and velocity. Never randomise pitch.",
  EARLY,ABL],
 [("Write the phrase in MIDI as a human would play it: small flams between chord notes, slightly off-grid timing and varied velocities so it does not sound computer-sequenced.","Piano roll","Natural-feeling 8-bar phrase"),
  ("Set the clip length one bar longer than the phrase (e.g. 9 bars for 8) and place a marker note at the very end of the extended region.","Piano roll","Clip has a spare bar and an end marker"),
  ("Switch to a triplet grid, draw one triplet note and stretch it until it spans the whole phrase, then select all and drag the clip's time-stretch handle until the end marker lines up with the last triplet hit. The phrase is now exactly 2/3 of its original length. Delete the triplet guide and marker notes.","Piano roll time-scale (MIDI stretch)","Phrase occupies 2/3 of original duration"),
  ("Select all notes and transpose up a perfect fifth (+7 semitones).","Piano roll","Notes 7 semitones higher, faster"),
  ("Resample the instrument to audio: record it onto an audio track set to resample the source (or freeze and flatten).","Bounce/resample","Audio clip of the fast, high version"),
  ("In the audio clip, turn warping off (repitch/varispeed playback) and transpose the clip down a perfect fifth (-7 semitones). Because 3:2 = a fifth, the clip returns to near-original tempo and pitch, now coloured by the resample.","Audio clip (warp off, transpose)","Original timing and pitch with a sampled-from-record texture"),
  ("Group the resampled track with a second audio track holding a very low-level noise bed. EQ out its low bumps and keep it far below the music.","Group + EQ","Subtle air/noise floor"),
  ("Glue the group with a gentle saturation/lo-fi colour stage (crackle set to zero) so the noise and part sound like one source. Repeat the whole process for the strings part.","Saturator / lo-fi colour","Cohesive resampled piano and strings layers")],
 ["Resampled clip length is within 1% of the original phrase length.","Pitch-detect on a held note matches the original MIDI pitch (within 10 cents) and shows no LFO pitch modulation.","Noise bed sits at least 25 dB below the part; no transient clicks are detected in it."],
 ["resampling","varispeed","lo-fi","piano","orchestral-strings","sample-manipulation","texture","midi"])

S("uZfNc_oCwOc","Ambient Composing Secrets: Scoring Under Dialogue For Film & TV",
 "drumless-emotional-ambient-cue-sneak-in-layers-high-cut-pads-reverse-delay-piano-artifacts-bass-entry-note-root-vs-flat-six-pulsing-piano-filter-revealed-texture-motif-ebb",
 "Drumless emotional ambient cue built one layer at a time: sneak-in entries, high-cut pads that leave the voice range clear, 100%-wet reverse-delay piano artifacts, a bass entry on the root (serious) or the flat-six (emotional), pulsing piano undertones, a filter-revealed texture loop and a modulation-ebbing motif",
 "Arrange a drumless ambient cue (a breakdown or underscore) that builds an emotional arc without drums. Each layer sneaks in quietly so the listener finds themselves immersed: an evolving bell-harmonic pad on one held tonic note with gentle 4th/5th/minor-3rd moves, high-cut so the upper harmonics stay below the dialogue or lead range; a slightly unsettling tension pad blended underneath; reversed piano 'artifacts' through a 100%-wet reverse delay playing in-key notes, with an auto-pan and an extra delay to lengthen them; a low pad whose entry note sets the emotion (tonic = dark/serious, flat-sixth e.g. Ab under C minor = emotional revelation); two piano layers (plain notes + a pulsing undertone figure) in shared reverb/delay; a soft breathy/formant texture pad and cinematic swells entering with the bass; a tempo-synced texture loop kept behind a closed low-pass and automated open only at moments; and a repeating synth motif that ebbs and flows through modulation automation. Delta vs the arrangement-ambient cluster (dark dialogue underscore in 8-bar sections, home-base excursions): emotional rather than tense, drumless, with the bass-entry-note emotion switch, reverse-delay artifacts and filter-revealed texture as the build tools.",
 ["A DAW with MIDI tracks, filter and volume automation","Pads (evolving bell/harmonic pad, tension pad, dark low pad, swells, breathy texture pad), a piano, a short sustained synth for the motif","A reverse delay (or reverse the delay return), a stereo auto-pan, a large reverb and a tempo-synced delay"],
 [("key","string","Minor key, e.g. C minor",True),("tempo_bpm","number","Slow, e.g. 60-80",False),("role","string","underscore (under dialogue/lead) or drumless breakdown inside a track",False)],
 [("cue","midi","Layered drumless cue: pad, tension pad, reverse artifacts, bass pad, two piano layers, texture pad, swells, filtered loop, motif"),("automation","string","Entry fades, low-pass reveal and motif modulation lanes")],
 ["Steady pitch: the reverse-delay piano plays a fixed in-key figure (root, minor 3rd, 5th, 7th) written as MIDI, not random hits; no pitch-modulated 'trembly' detune on the tension pad. Use slow volume/filter movement instead (Matt dislikes wobbly/random pitch variation).",
  "No rapid clicking/stutter textures: the pulsing piano undertone is slow (quarter or half notes) and soft-attack; reverse artifacts are long, not granular ticks.",
  "Leave 1-4 kHz light for the voice (dialogue or lead): high-cut pads and keep the arrangement thin.",
  "The bass entry note is a deliberate emotional choice: tonic for a serious/dark mood, the flat-sixth below the tonic for an emotional lift. Choose per section.",
  "The vocal-library texture is generalised to a soft breathy/formant pad. No vocal production is involved.",
  "Product and library names from the transcript are not needed; any pad and piano with comparable character works.",
  "Drumless by design. When used as a breakdown inside a beat track, the drums still enter early in the track (~8 counts / ~12 s) and return after this section (Matt's preference).",ABL],
 [("Start with an evolving bell-harmonic pad holding the tonic (e.g. middle C). Fade it in so the entry is barely noticed, and move gently to the 4th, 5th or minor 3rd. Add a high-cut filter so the upper harmonics sit below the voice/lead range.","Pad + low-pass EQ + volume automation","Quiet, evolving tonic bed with no bright top"),
  ("Blend in a slightly unsettling tension pad under the first pad as the baseline texture.","Pad (blend)","Subtle unease under the bed"),
  ("Add reversed piano artifacts: put a piano through a reverse delay at 100% wet (only the reversed signal), follow with an auto-panner, a large reverb and a delay to lengthen them, and play an in-key figure (root, minor 3rd, 5th, 7th).","Piano + reverse delay + auto-pan + reverb + delay","Soft reversed swells that add pacing and ear candy"),
  ("Introduce the low end with a dark low pad. Enter on the tonic for weight and seriousness, or on the flat-sixth (Ab under C minor) for a more emotional, revelatory turn.","Low pad, MIDI note choice","Arc gains weight. Entry note sets the emotion"),
  ("Tie the layers with two piano parts: a plain sustained note layer and a slow pulsing undertone figure, both sent to the shared reverb/delay.","Piano x2 + reverb/delay sends","Gentle pulse without drums"),
  ("Add a distinctive soft breathy/formant texture pad woven in and out, and bring in cinematic swells at the same moment as the bass pad, playing in-key harmonies.","Texture pad + swell pad","Arc widens as the low end arrives"),
  ("Drop in a tempo-synced texture loop behind a low-pass filter closed almost fully. Automate the cutoff open only where extra texture is wanted, and add delay to blend it.","Audio loop + low-pass automation + delay","Texture appears quietly at chosen moments"),
  ("Finish with a short repeating synth motif. Automate its modulation (filter/brightness/level) so it pokes in and out and reverbs away into the other layers. Give each layer its own moment to enter and breathe before the next.","Synth + modulation automation","Cohesive drumless cue with a clear emotional arc")],
 ["No drum tracks are present in the cue section.","Each layer's first 2 s is at least 6 dB below its later level (sneak-in entry).","Pad layers' energy above ~4 kHz is at least 12 dB below 500 Hz-2 kHz (high-cut applied).","The bass pad's first note is the tonic or the flat-sixth of the key, as chosen."],
 ["arrangement","ambient","drumless","breakdown","underscore","cinematic","reverse-delay","bass-entry","emotional-arc"])
